course: dictionary
lesson: 7582
title: Prevent: stopping things before they start
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To prevent something means to stop it from happening. Prevent is about getting in first, before the problem starts. «A clear family rule about buying, such as one purchase a month, prevents most arguments.» The rule does not end an argument that has already started. It stops most arguments from happening at all.
explain: To prevent someone from doing something means to stop them doing it. «Riders wear helmets on every horse, because helmets prevent many serious head injuries.» Swap your meaning into the sentence: helmets stop many serious head injuries from happening. It still makes sense, so you have understood prevent.
explain: Prevent is a verb, so it changes its ending: prevent, prevents, prevented, preventing. Look at the time in the sentence. «Last year the dam prevented the town from flooding.» The dam worked in the past, so prevented is the right form.
fact: Prevent is a verb: prevent, prevents, prevented, preventing.
fact: «Prevent» means to stop something from happening.
fact: To prevent someone from doing something means to stop them doing it.
fact: «Prevention is better than cure» is a saying that means it is easier to stop a problem than to fix it later.
fact: In health lessons, we wash hands to prevent germs spreading and wear sun cream to prevent sunburn.
exercise: «Riders wear helmets on every horse, because helmets prevent many serious head injuries.» What does prevent mean here? | Make helmets heavier | *Stop serious head injuries from happening | Ride faster | Cause serious head injuries
exercise: Mum says, «Wash your hands to prevent germs spreading.» What is the purpose of washing hands? | To make germs grow faster | To spread germs to everyone | *To stop germs from spreading
exercise: Fill the gap: «Last year, the dam ___ the town from flooding.» | prevents | preventing | *prevented | prevent
test: «A banana is a good snack, but it does not prevent cramp in sport for most people.» Does a banana stop cramp for most people? | Yes, always | It makes cramp worse | Only in the morning | *No, it does not stop cramp for most people
test: Which saying means it is easier to stop a problem than to fix it later? | The early bird catches the worm | *Prevention is better than cure | Many hands make light work | Practice makes perfect
exam: «Gorillas beat their chests, and this often prevents fights.» What does prevents mean? | *Stops fights from happening | Starts fights | Makes fights louder | Watches fights
